// The saddle go module marker (the goget wave): the engine envelope
// rides the go get rung the way it rides the maven, nuget, rubygems and
// gradle rungs — the module path answers the
// github.com/wenathlan/devthink monorepo with the per-application
// subdirectory and the major version suffix the go semver law demands
// at the v2 line, and the version answers the per-module tag
// (saddle/vX.Y.Z on the release commit) the publish lane syncs — the go
// module registry carries no version literal the rung ladder would have
// to stamp, the same way the gradle marker reads the envelope
// package.json at build time.
//
// The module owns the whole saddle envelope (the go module zip carries
// every tracked file under the app root the way the family source
// tarball does — the documentation set, the tests, the sol interface and
// the engine sources beside them) while its one go package — the module
// identity carrier below — lives in the documentation support seat at
// docs/: the app root carries the C engine sources (virtualhardware.c
// beside the virtualization core and the gpu monitor companions) the go
// package law refuses inside a package directory, and the flat layout
// law keeps the app root to the sol interface and the support seats, so
// the doc carrier rides the one seat both laws keep for it.
module github.com/wenathlan/devthink/saddle/v2

go 1.27
